.SH "Field Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::echo_removal_db"
Most the residual echo is pushed down by, in decibels, negative\&. Default -40\&. This is what is left after the canceller has done its work, so it is a safety net rather than the main mechanism\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB232\fP of file \fBschultz_voice\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::echo_removal_talking_db"
The same, for while the person at this end is talking\&. Default -15\&. Less, on purpose: pushing hard here is what makes somebody sound cut off when both people speak at once\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB238\fP of file \fBschultz_voice\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::noise_removal_db"
Most the background noise is pushed down by, in decibels, negative\&. Default -15\&. The one people actually reach for\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB243\fP of file \fBschultz_voice\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::gain_target"
How loud automatic gain aims for, as a fraction of full scale from zero to one\&. Default 0\&.244, which is speexdsp's 8000 out of 32768\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB248\fP of file \fBschultz_voice\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::gain_ceiling_db"
Most gain it is allowed to add, in decibels\&. Default 30\&. A ceiling matters: without one, a silent room gets its hiss amplified until it hits the target\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB254\fP of file \fBschultz_voice\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::detection_start"
How sure detection has to be before it calls something speech, as a percentage from zero to a hundred\&. Default 35\&. 
.PP
Definition at line \fB259\fP of file \fBschultz_voice\&.h\fP\&.
.SS "float schultz_voice_tuning::detection_continue"
How sure it has to stay to go on calling it speech\&. Default 20, lower than the start on purpose: it makes detection hold through the quiet parts of a word instead of chopping it up\&. 
.PP
